{
  "rationale": "The spec is area-constrained with a modest accuracy requirement (max_abs_err <= 2^-10) and a low throughput floor (>= 1 MSPS). Iterative CORDIC reuses a single datapath and is therefore the most area-efficient family; unrolled_k replicates the datapath k times, increasing area, so it is likely dominated. We focus the search on data_width 12..18 and n_iter 10..20, since W < 12 cannot meet the output LSB requirement (2^-(W-2) > 2^-10) and N < 10 cannot meet the angle resolution. Guards are searched in a narrow range around 0 to find the minimum area that still meets error. Rounding is included because it can improve accuracy at little area cost. The throughput constraint is easily met even for N=20 (Fmax/(N+3) >> 1 MSPS), so it does not further restrict the ranges.",
  "families": [
    {
      "why": "Primary family for minimum area. Ranges cover the feasible accuracy region with minimal area: W >= 12 for output LSB, N >= 10 for angle resolution, and small guard ranges to find the area-accuracy knee. Rounding is included as a cheap accuracy improvement.",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 18
        ,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "param": "n_iter",
          "low": 10,
          "high": 20,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "param": "angle_guard",
          "low": -2,
          "high": 2,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "param": "frac_guard",
          "low": 0,
          "high": 2,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
          "param": "rounding",
          "low": null,
          "high": null,
          "choices": ["trunc", "round"]
        }
      ],
      "family": "iterative",
      "budget_share": 0.85
    },
    {
      "why": "Probe for any unexpected area/throughput trade-off. k > 1 increases area, so we restrict k to 2..4 to limit wasted budget. If no point appears on the Pareto front, this family is confirmed dominated.",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 18,
          "choices": null
